\label{thm:dim_count_CT}
    Let $\vec{\theta}=(\theta_1, \cdots, \theta_n) \in \mathbb{R}^n_+$ be an angle vector with $\theta_i\neq1$ and $\vec{T}=( E,\emptyset, N )$ be a type partition with $ \#E=n_E, \#N=n_N $.
    Whenever $\mathcal{M}sph_{g,n}^C(\vec{\theta};\vec{T})$ is non-empty, its real dimension is given by the following:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $g>0$, the dimension is $2n_E+2g-1$;
        \item If $g=0$ and $N$ non-empty, the dimension is $2n_E-1$;
        \item If $g=0$ and $N$ empty, then $\vec{\theta}\in\mathbb{N}_{>1}^n$ and the dimension is $2n-3$.
    \end{itemize}

